            "review_title": "Review at Quan Bia Minh",
            "review_text": "DaleB\nMelbourne, Australia221 contributions\n0\nGood location and cold beer, average food\nJan 2020\nI ate here on my last night in Hanoi. I was on my own so sat upstairs on the balcony overlooking the busy street below. \nI ordered a beer and started with the pork spring rolls, which were really delicious. I ate a lot of spring rolls in Vietnam and these ones were up there with the best. \nFor main meal I ordered a beef dish with chilli and lemongrass and was disappointed. I was served a huge plate of onion, with beef and carrot scattered throughout. Unfortunately I’m not a fan of onion, so I found myself picking around it. The flavour was a bit bland also. \n\nHad I just had beer and spring rolls, it would have been much better.\nRead more\nWritten January 8, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
